      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both ACE inhibitors and ARBs are recommended as top-choice, first-line treatments for high blood pressure, but ARBs are often preferred today because they have fewer side effects.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "ARBs are often preferred today because they have fewer side effects"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How They Work"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "ACE inhibitors (like lisinopril) stop your body from making a hormone that narrows your blood vessels."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "(like losartan) block that same hormone from attaching to your blood vessels."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Both relax your blood vessels to lower your blood pressure."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Differences"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Effectiveness: Large studies show both drug classes lower blood pressure and protect your heart and kidneys just as well."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Side Effects: ACE inhibitors often cause a nagging, dry cough and carry a small risk of dangerous swelling called angioedema. ARBs do not build up the chemical that causes this cough, making them much better tolerated by patients."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cost: ACE inhibitors are usually available as older, lower-cost generics, though many ARBs are also affordable now ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to discuss this with your doctor, would you like to know more about:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Common side effects to watch out for"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Specific names of medications in each class"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Which one fits best if you have kidney disease or diabetes?"
          }
        ]
      }
